  "notes": "Composed of {誤|ご} (mistake, error) + {認|にん} (recognition). A formal word indicating that someone has incorrectly identified or perceived something. Frequently appears in news reporting, especially regarding police and legal matters.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {誤認|ごにん}{逮捕|たいほ}: wrongful arrest\n- {誤認|ごにん}{請求|せいきゅう}: billing error; mistaken claim\n- {人物|じんぶつ}{誤認|ごにん}: misidentification of a person\n- {事実|じじつ}{誤認|ごにん}: factual error\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {誤解|ごかい}: misunderstanding (about meaning or intent, more conversational)\n- {見間違|みまちが}い: seeing incorrectly, visual mistake (everyday language)\n- {勘違|かんちが}い: misunderstanding, wrong assumption (casual, common)",
